WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.290
- She's one of our favorites at this show.

00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:04.770
Her new podcast is called Bunga Bunga.

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:08.382
It's about Italian
Dictator Silvio Berlusconi.

00:00:08.382 --> 00:00:09.680
Because why not?

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:12.465
Sure, give it up for
Whitney Cummings everybody.

00:00:12.465 --> 00:00:14.845
(audience applauds)

00:00:14.845 --> 00:00:17.428
(upbeat music)

00:00:28.064 --> 00:00:29.064
- Oh hi, hi!

00:00:29.978 --> 00:00:32.822
(Whitney screams)

00:00:32.822 --> 00:00:34.404
- So awkward.
- Hi everyone!

00:00:34.404 --> 00:00:35.698
- You are so cute!

00:00:35.698 --> 00:00:38.170
- I do look cute.
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:39.820
Don't I look cute?

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:43.185
I have not left the house in six months.

00:00:43.185 --> 00:00:44.400
(Kelly laughs loudly)

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:47.310
So I just want everyone to take this in.

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:50.155
I just really wanna
appreciate this moment.

00:00:50.155 --> 00:00:54.336
Oh, hey boys, hey boys, hey there.

00:00:54.336 --> 00:00:55.400
- You're magical!

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:58.010
I feel like how you're energy just was,

00:00:58.010 --> 00:00:59.967
was how everyone feels
about their life right now.

00:00:59.967 --> 00:01:02.800
Your just out of your house.
- I've gone insane!

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:04.380
I mean, I've truly gone insane.

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:06.219
'Member Jack Nicholson
at the end of the movie?

00:01:06.219 --> 00:01:07.800
That like me.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.380
I just remembered to cross my legs.

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:11.210
I haven't been out of
the house in six months.

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:12.403
I was like, "Cross your legs."

00:01:12.403 --> 00:01:15.781
It's the first time I've worn
a thong in truly four months.

00:01:15.781 --> 00:01:16.614
(Kelly laughs and claps)

00:01:16.614 --> 00:01:17.447
Have you guys worn one?

00:01:17.447 --> 00:01:18.990
It's like sawing through my body.

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:20.650
I forgot how painful these are.

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:22.550
- Well, I'm sorry I'm wearing a patch.

00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:24.750
I hurt my eye, some weird
infection, whatever.

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:26.560
- I saw it, we should get you that bird

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:27.570
and put it on your shoulders.

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:29.465
So you'll look like Captain Morgan.

00:01:29.465 --> 00:01:30.298
(Kelly laughs loudly)

00:01:30.298 --> 00:01:31.620
- I'll take the alcohol.

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:32.910
Okay, no, you're hysterical.

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:35.940
No but you have pets, right?
- I do, i have so man pets.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:37.810
- Do you have any pets
with like, awesome things,

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:38.800
like Tico the parrot?

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:41.020
- I don't have a parrot like Tico.

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:44.470
Although I do look like a
tropical bird now with this vibe.

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:47.880
I have three dogs, I have
a pig, and I have horse.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:49.710
So--
- You're like a farm girl?

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:50.790
- I am like a farm girl.

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:52.278
I feel like that equals one child.

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:53.243
Is that fair?

00:01:54.286 --> 00:01:56.923
- It depends on the child.
(Whitney laughs loudly)

00:01:56.923 --> 00:01:59.990
- So yes, I do have animals.

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:00.823
I love them.

00:02:00.823 --> 00:02:02.940
It's like having kids, but
they can't, like talk back.

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:04.612
And you don't have--
- It's the best!

00:02:04.612 --> 00:02:06.190
Best relationship.
- Yeah, you can't like,

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:08.010
you can put 'em in like a crate 'til--

00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:08.843
- Right.

00:02:08.843 --> 00:02:10.100
- Best version--
- Well, there are cribs.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:11.310
But yeah.
( Whitney laughs)

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:13.150
- I guess it is similar.

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:16.280
No but Tico, have you been
trying to be an influencer?

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:17.700
I've seen this, I follow you.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:19.259
You're hysterical.
- I am hysterical.

00:02:19.259 --> 00:02:20.988
- You are, you are!
(Whitney laughs loudly)

00:02:20.988 --> 00:02:23.570
I'm telling you, and I am being honest.

00:02:23.570 --> 00:02:26.650
Like, in such a hard
summer for a lot of us,

00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:28.530
it's such nice escapism.

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:30.520
Humor is so healing.
- So healing.

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:33.584
- I'm not joking, I literally
go on Twitter to find you,

00:02:33.584 --> 00:02:36.378
just to read your stuff
when I'm having a crap day.

00:02:36.378 --> 00:02:38.600
- I love you!
- No, 'cause it's funny,

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:39.980
and it's nice, and it's hopeful,

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:41.350
'cause it's like, "Okay, we're gonna laugh

00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:43.220
again at some point."
- There's this narrative

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:44.930
that like, the country's so divided.

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:45.910
And everyone hates each other.

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:46.970
I don't believe that.

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:49.260
I think there is a lot of that out there.

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:51.440
But I think that, you
know, I love doing standup,

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:53.250
because you get a bunch
of people in a room

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:54.230
that don't know each other.

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:55.319
And probably voted differently.

00:02:55.319 --> 00:02:57.492
And they can all laugh at
the same stuff, you know.

00:02:57.492 --> 00:02:59.050
- That's how if feel about concerts.

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:00.060
I think when people--
- Yes, that's what music

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:01.560
does too, it brings people together.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:04.758
And you know, so during this time,

00:03:04.758 --> 00:03:07.155
I've been getting very risky

00:03:07.155 --> 00:03:09.700
in some of the videos
and stuff we're making.

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:12.200
Just to try to make you
guys laugh at all costs.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:13.783
Benton, my assistant has been putting

00:03:13.783 --> 00:03:17.250
me in danger constantly, to try
to make funny TikTok videos.

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:18.242
- I was gonna say, you're TikTok videos,

00:03:18.242 --> 00:03:20.340
the one with the wine
was one of my favorites.

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:21.430
When you were drinking--
- Well, all of

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:22.990
my TikTok videos involve wine.

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:25.250
But that one, I just drink it on camera.

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:26.801
Oh yes, there it is!
- This is my favorite.

00:03:26.801 --> 00:03:29.168
- So this is a TikTok challenge,

00:03:29.168 --> 00:03:32.410
where you try to like, sorta
like put the wine in your mouth

00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:33.510
and the other person drinks it.

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:34.970
I didn't like it 'cause I like the wine

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:36.892
to get down my gullet
as quickly as possible.

00:03:36.892 --> 00:03:38.190
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:40.080
And yeah, so Benton
keeps putting me in all

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:42.460
these like crazy dangerous
TikTok challenges.

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:44.910
Which a lot of 'em are
actually very scary.

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:46.030
And I have to tell 'em, "Look, you know

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:47.340
you're not in my will, right?"

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:50.062
If I die, I don't know why
you're tryna kill me to much.

00:03:50.062 --> 00:03:53.460
Guys, my eyelashes just came out.

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:54.820
- Your eyelash just came out?

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:58.220
- Yeah, oops, I think I
need and eye patch too.

00:03:58.220 --> 00:03:59.300
- You want one?
- I was so jealous

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:00.268
that you had one.
- You just wanted

00:04:00.268 --> 00:04:02.290
to be like me.
- What do I do

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:03.140
if my eyelashes come out?

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:04.770
- You should just--
- Do I have to take

00:04:04.770 --> 00:04:05.603
the other one out?

00:04:05.603 --> 00:04:06.436
Do I look crazy?
- I actually can't tell.

00:04:06.436 --> 00:04:07.626
- I mean, compare to you, probably not.

00:04:07.626 --> 00:04:10.455
(Kelly laughs loudly)

00:04:10.455 --> 00:04:12.452
- Compared to me, you look great!

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:14.980
- I'll just leave my eyelashes right here.

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:16.258
- Just leave 'em there.
- I have not left

00:04:16.258 --> 00:04:17.560
the house in so long.
- Do you feel like

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:18.580
we're playing some kind of game,

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:20.113
where we're slowly
undressing when we lose?

00:04:20.113 --> 00:04:22.394
(Whitney laughs loudly)

00:04:22.394 --> 00:04:25.495
- Wait, speaking of undressing,
how's your dating life?

00:04:25.495 --> 00:04:28.370
- My dating life is ridiculous.

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:29.690
Pretty usual, but it seems like the guy

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:30.523
with the bird single.

00:04:30.523 --> 00:04:32.940
So I feel like I have
that, maybe on the horizon.

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:36.980
I started dating online in quarantine,

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:37.930
which everybody is doing.

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:39.869
And I have to be honest with
you, I'm not against it.

00:04:39.869 --> 00:04:42.260
So you have to do first dates now

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:43.960
like on FaceTime, yah know?

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:45.520
Which I thought was
gonna be really annoying.

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:46.910
But it's my new favorite thing.

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:48.880
- I feel like that's awkward.
- No, 'cause you can see

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:50.680
the inside of their house right away.

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:53.490
You can see their bathroom
on the first date,

00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:56.385
which you couldn't do
before, unless you're a--

00:04:56.385 --> 00:04:58.711
- Psycho!
(Whitney laughs)

00:04:58.711 --> 00:05:00.860
- She's gonna say psycho,
I was gonna say slut.

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:01.920
But--
- Okay.

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:02.753
- You're--
- Oh, I just thought

00:05:02.753 --> 00:05:03.800
you meant creeping in their stuff.

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:05.860
Oh okay.
- Because I can't go to a

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:08.939
guys house on the first
date, 'cause I'm a lady.

00:05:08.939 --> 00:05:10.150
(Kelly laughs loudly)

00:05:10.150 --> 00:05:11.257
But this way, you can be like,

00:05:11.257 --> 00:05:13.050
"Hey, like let me see your bathroom."

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:14.869
And you can go in, and
you can truly find out

00:05:14.869 --> 00:05:16.570
if they actually dating someone or not.

00:05:16.570 --> 00:05:18.370
'Cause a lot of times guys
will say they're single,

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:20.700
but they're still
getting out of something.

00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:22.140
- There's a word for that, lying?

00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:23.366
- Lying?
(Whitney laughs)

00:05:23.366 --> 00:05:25.480
Show me your shower, I will tell you

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:26.990
if you're still in a relationship or not.

00:05:26.990 --> 00:05:29.592
If there's one little
sliver of Irish Spring,

00:05:29.592 --> 00:05:32.580
like a little piece of bark and that's it.

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:34.262
You're single, I believe you.

00:05:34.262 --> 00:05:37.750
If I see some pink Bath and Body Works.

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:41.459
Moonlit path, shave, you're
still in a relationship.

00:05:41.459 --> 00:05:42.573
I'm , you're blocked.

00:05:43.523 --> 00:05:45.560
- Wait, so how is comedy going now?

00:05:45.560 --> 00:05:46.980
'Cause like, can you still do comedy?

00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:48.330
Do you go to, 'cause I remember last time.

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:49.163
This was such a funny.

00:05:49.163 --> 00:05:51.200
You used to talk about, you're
a little bit of a germophobe.

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:52.033
You used to carry your own mic.

00:05:52.033 --> 00:05:53.350
- Yes!
- So you were ahead

00:05:53.350 --> 00:05:54.183
of the the curve.
- I can't believe

00:05:54.183 --> 00:05:55.720
you remember this.
- We actually were talking

00:05:55.720 --> 00:05:57.620
about it, because I
remember, like, she was way

00:05:57.620 --> 00:05:58.453
ahead of the curve.

00:05:58.453 --> 00:06:00.003
And I thought Howie Mandel,
you would get along.

00:06:00.003 --> 00:06:01.390
(Kelly and Whitney laugh)

00:06:01.390 --> 00:06:02.640
'Cause he's pretty much like that.

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:05.700
- Well, the last time I saw
you I was promoting a tour,

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:07.016
that unfortunately got canceled.

00:06:07.016 --> 00:06:09.644
And I was talking about
how I was so neurotic,

00:06:09.644 --> 00:06:12.530
because I brought my own
microphone to every gig.

00:06:12.530 --> 00:06:14.360
'Cause I didn't wanna get sick.

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:16.530
So my tour has been canceled, as you know.

00:06:16.530 --> 00:06:17.843
So much live stuff has been canceled.

00:06:17.843 --> 00:06:19.520
I just book a bunch of dates.

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:21.392
We're gonna be doing comedy outside.

00:06:21.392 --> 00:06:24.200
We're gonna be doing some
drive-in comedy shows.

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:26.670
I'm so glad you guys are clapping,

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:28.950
because we're trying so
hard to make this work.

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:29.783
- Yeah.
- Find a way

00:06:29.783 --> 00:06:32.405
to come make you guys laugh,
and come to your city.

00:06:32.405 --> 00:06:35.610
You, thank you, I'm a hero!

00:06:35.610 --> 00:06:36.773
I agree!
(Kelly laughs)

00:06:36.773 --> 00:06:39.519
I fixed America!
- I'm a surgeon!

00:06:39.519 --> 00:06:42.790
- But you, I mean, as a
musician you perform outside

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:44.020
all the time?
- Yeah.

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:46.410
- And it's, it's not really,
it doesn't really come natural

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:47.770
to comedians, so I don't know what to say.

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:50.491
I'm like, "Bring your
Lunchables and your bug spray."

00:06:50.491 --> 00:06:52.963
- Okay wait!
(Kelly laughs)

00:06:52.963 --> 00:06:55.620
How have you been getting
human interaction?

00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:57.043
I feel like you've been getting a lot.

00:06:57.043 --> 00:06:58.210
(Kelly and Whitney laugh)

00:06:58.210 --> 00:07:03.020
- I am so crazy, guys, I forgot
how to talk to human beings.

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:05.260
- No you don't, I watch
the podcast, you're funny.

00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:06.710
So Bunga Bunga, tell us, yeah.

00:07:06.710 --> 00:07:09.331
- What, what, yes, I'm just kidding.

00:07:09.331 --> 00:07:11.890
- No you're Bunga Bunga, tell us about it.

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:12.723
And why?

00:07:12.723 --> 00:07:14.240
It's so random.
- Yes, it's so random.

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:16.031
You're intro was like,
"Bunga Bunga, why not?"

00:07:16.031 --> 00:07:20.050
Bunga Bunga: So I don't
know if you guys have heard

00:07:20.050 --> 00:07:21.026
Wondery does these podcast.

00:07:21.026 --> 00:07:23.940
Like, you've seen Dirty John, Dr. Death.

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:28.240
They do these like really cool
like murder mystery podcasts.

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:30.700
And they asked me to host one of them,

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:32.950
which is so weird because
men always tell me

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:34.101
they don't wanna hear my voice.

00:07:34.101 --> 00:07:35.886
(Kelly laughs loudly)

00:07:35.886 --> 00:07:37.578
Certainly, not more than five minutes.

00:07:37.578 --> 00:07:39.060
This is an eight hour show.

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:41.270
So I tried to make
myself like, less shrill,

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:43.870
and kind of like sexy and
sultry when I did the narrating.

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:46.167
- Don't do that for you.
- It's really wasn't (laughs).

00:07:46.167 --> 00:07:47.896
(Whitney screams)
The Fran Drescher impression.

00:07:47.896 --> 00:07:50.874
And so, it's about this
guy Silvio Berlusconi.

00:07:50.874 --> 00:07:54.210
Who is this dictator that did
all this incredible stuff.

00:07:54.210 --> 00:07:55.950
Just listen to it, you'll
be the smartest person

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:56.783
at the dinner party.

00:07:56.783 --> 00:07:58.210
If for nothing else, do it just

00:07:58.210 --> 00:07:59.043
to be better than your friends.

00:07:59.043 --> 00:07:59.876
- That's so cool!

00:07:59.876 --> 00:08:00.709
How random, that you got
asked to do that, right?

00:08:00.709 --> 00:08:02.480
- Well, it was very, very random.

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:04.920
He had lots of dalliances with women.

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:07.430
Some of them untoward, some of them,

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:09.100
he was kind of a sketchy dude.

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:11.574
So I think that bringing
me on, I found a way

00:08:11.574 --> 00:08:16.220
to tell the story while
not judging him too much.

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:18.450
But also holding him
accountable for his behavior.

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:19.850
It's a really interesting story

00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:22.210
about a man that abused his power,

00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:24.520
and brainwashed a country.

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:26.490
And it's kind of a great way for us to all

00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:28.289
like you know, ask more questions.

00:08:28.289 --> 00:08:31.238
And as women, look at the men above us,

00:08:31.238 --> 00:08:34.220
and say, "No thanks, cut it out."

00:08:34.220 --> 00:08:35.860
- Yeah, and it's okay to say that.

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:37.517
- Yes, it is okay to say that.
- Yes, yes.

00:08:37.517 --> 00:08:39.885
Well, be sure to keep
an eye out for Whitney's

00:08:39.885 --> 00:08:42.721
Codependent Tour and
check out her new podcast.

00:08:42.721 --> 00:08:44.730
It's called Bunga Bunga.

00:08:44.730 --> 00:08:46.853
You can find it wherever
you get your podcasts.

